            <ArticleTitle>Myoepithelial carcinoma in the mediastinum involving the left atrium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>158-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carpath.2015.09.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1054-8807(15)00112-X</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 56-year-old male who presented with typical atrial flutter and was diagnosed with a large mediastinal mass, posterior to the ascending aorta, noted within the left atrium, compressing the superior vena cava and right superior pulmonary vein, and measuring &gt;9.0 cm at its greatest diameter. Histopathological studies showed a myoepithelial carcinoma. The patient underwent tumor debulking and radiation therapy. This is the first report of a mediastinal myoepithelial carcinoma involving cardiac chambers.</AbstractText>
